This project is a combination of components licensed under different terms:

1. The core emulator logic (native code in app/cpp/native_core) is derived from Opera upstream sources. This code is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License version 2.1 (LGPL v2.1). The project is named Retro-3DO and is not derived from the former 4DO Android frontend.

2. The Android-specific frontend, UI code, renderer integration, launcher, game library, IGDB integration, bezel handling, controller mapping, artwork, and project-specific code (unless otherwise specified) are licensed under the MIT License.

3. The complete corresponding source for the Opera-derived native core and this project's local modifications is available in this repository, as LGPL v2.1 requires.

4. IMPORTANT — the LGPL is not the whole picture for the native core. Seven files under app/cpp/native_core/ (native_madam.c, native_arm.c, native_dsp.c, native_cdrom.c, native_clio.c, native_3do.c, native_sport.c) carry the FreeDO notice, which states that commercial use is "strictly forbidden without owners approval" and that "the above notes are taking precedence over GNU LGPL in conflicting situations".

   An earlier version of this file stated that commercial distribution was permitted under LGPL v2.1. That was not correct while those files are present: the addendum in them explicitly overrides the LGPL where the two conflict, and permission to sell is such a conflict.

   The remaining native code and the entire Android application are unaffected and are MIT / LGPL as described above.

   See docs/PROVENANCE.md for the full position, which files are affected, and the work to replace them with clean-room implementations.

